{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_001","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"JSON Schema - Specification [#section]","location_hint":"paragraph 1","char_start":0,"char_end":38,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_002","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"Specification Docs Tools Blog Community","location_hint":"paragraph 2","char_start":48,"char_end":87,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_003","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"The current version is 2020-12 !\nThe previous version was 2019-09.","location_hint":"paragraph 20","char_start":354,"char_end":420,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_004","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"See also the release notes / change log (Work in progress).","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":447,"char_end":506,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_005","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"The specification is split into two parts, Core and Validation. We also publish\nthe Relative JSON Pointers spec although it&#x27;s not currently used by Core or\nValidation in any significant way.","location_hint":"paragraph 23","char_start":508,"char_end":703,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_006","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"JSON Schema Core defines the basic foundation of JSON Schema","location_hint":"paragraph 24","char_start":711,"char_end":771,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_007","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"JSON Schema Validation defines the validation keywords of JSON Schema","location_hint":"paragraph 25","char_start":773,"char_end":842,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_008","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"Relative JSON Pointers extends the JSON Pointer syntax for relative pointers","location_hint":"paragraph 26","char_start":844,"char_end":920,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_009","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"The meta-schemas are schemas against which other schemas can be validated. It is self-descriptive: the JSON Schema meta-schema validates itself.","location_hint":"paragraph 28","char_start":938,"char_end":1082,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_010","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"The latest meta-schema is 2020-12 . For an explanation of the change to date-based identifiers, see the Specification Links page.","location_hint":"paragraph 29","char_start":1084,"char_end":1213,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_011","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"If you are accessing these JSON document links from a web browser , you will need to save the file then open it as a JSON document. This is due to limitations with GitHub Pages.","location_hint":"paragraph 30","char_start":1215,"char_end":1392,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_012","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"Please note, additional vocabulary specific schema files are needed to fully construct and use the Core/Validation Dialect meta-schema.","location_hint":"paragraph 32","char_start":1423,"char_end":1558,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_013","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"Core/Validation Dialect meta-schema Used for schemas written for pure validation.","location_hint":"paragraph 33","char_start":1566,"char_end":1647,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b1ed6cf92876_014","source_id":"src_b1ed6cf92876","source_hash":"d3a5677e4c094f7bbca48e8da2b06659191b19da035f449d9cf103ee3944db7f","text":"Hyper-Schema Dialect meta-schema Used for schemas written for validation (2020-12) and hyper-linking (2019-09).","location_hint":"paragraph 34","char_start":1649,"char_end":1760,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:27:28.759Z"}
